// Figure 4.6 — Activity diagram: analyst alert review workflow (swimlanes as groups)
// Eraser: New diagram > Flow chart, paste this code.
direction right

Analyst [color: blue] {
  Start [shape: oval, color: black, label: ""]
  Open alerts queue [icon: list]
  Filter by status and sort [icon: filter]
  Open an alert [icon: eye]
  Study score + explanation + features [icon: search]
  Is it fraud? [shape: diamond, color: yellow]
  Confirm fraud with note [color: red]
  Mark false positive with note [color: green]
  End [shape: oval, color: black, label: ""]
}

System [color: purple] {
  Show live queue of open alerts [icon: monitor]
  Compute or load explanation [icon: cpu]
  Alert still open or user is admin? [shape: diamond, color: yellow]
  Refuse with 403 [color: red]
  Update alert + counters + audit log [icon: database]
  Push update to every dashboard [icon: radio]
}

Start > Open alerts queue
Open alerts queue > Show live queue of open alerts
Show live queue of open alerts > Filter by status and sort
Filter by status and sort > Open an alert
Open an alert > Compute or load explanation
Compute or load explanation > Study score + explanation + features
Study score + explanation + features > Is it fraud?
Is it fraud? > Confirm fraud with note: yes
Is it fraud? > Mark false positive with note: no
Confirm fraud with note > Alert still open or user is admin?
Mark false positive with note > Alert still open or user is admin?
Alert still open or user is admin? > Refuse with 403: no
Alert still open or user is admin? > Update alert + counters + audit log: yes
Update alert + counters + audit log > Push update to every dashboard
Push update to every dashboard > End
Refuse with 403 > End
